Tracker: GitHub (engineering-loop's github.md)

## Components

Where a change lands: one bullet per component, its label `area:<name>` in
backticks, then what it covers. Every issue carries at least one. Edit the list
to the project's parts; `mise run setup:github` creates each label.

{% for name, text in components %}- `area:{{ name }}`: {{ text }}
{% endfor %}- `area:tooling`: mise tasks, git hooks, CI workflows and agent configuration
- `area:docs`: the README and the docs outside `docs/agents/`

## Never on GitHub

What must never appear in an issue, comment, commit message or PR, such as
customer data, credentials or private figures, and what to write instead.
"None" is an answer.

## Extra labels

Optional. Labels this project adds beyond the pack's: one bullet per label, its
name in backticks, then what it means.

## Extra categories

Optional. Categories beyond the method's four (`kind:bug`, `kind:enhancement`,
`kind:chore`, `kind:documentation`): one bullet per category, its label
`kind:<name>` in backticks, then what it means.

## Renamed labels

Optional. Labels to rename in place, so every issue keeps them: one bullet per
label, its old name then its new, both in backticks, such as `frontend` becomes
`area:web`. The pack's own renames (`bug`, `enhancement`, `chore` and
`documentation` to their `kind:` names) need no line.

## Board

The board column each loop column shows in, one bullet each: the loop column,
then the board's, both in backticks. Rename the second to the board's own
column; several loop columns may share one, and a loop column left out keeps
its own name.

- `Intent` is `Intent`
- `Needs owner` is `Needs owner`
- `Ready` is `Ready`
- `Build` is `Build`
- `Verify` is `Verify`
- `Sign-off` is `Sign-off`
- `Done` is `Done`
